  "result": "The issue has been fixed. The vulnerability was in the `findIssueById` function in `/src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts`. \n\nThe function was accepting an `orgId` parameter but not actually using it when querying the database. This allowed a user from one organization to fetch an issue belonging to a completely different organization by providing only the issue ID.\n\nThe fix adds the organization scope check to the query using `orgPredicate(issues.orgId, orgId)`, ensuring that issues can only be retrieved if they belong to the specified organization. This matches the correct pattern already implemented in the `findIssueByNumber` function in the same file.\n\nNow when a user from Organization A attempts to access an issue ID from Organization B, the query will return `null` and the application will behave as if the issue doesn't exist, properly enforcing tenant isolation.",
